I've shown [here](https://stackoverflow.com/a/46992682/2545680) where the leaks come from. Basically these are:

```
export class JitCompiler {
  private _compiledHostTemplateCache = new Map<Type, CompiledTemplate>();
```
and 

```
const _tokenKeyCache = new Map<any, string>();
```
The `DynamicHtmlComponent` and `DynamicHtmlComponentFactory` are used as keys in those maps and hence the references are still retained after the component is destroyed.

@RajkumarSiva , has there been any progress on this issue? My team is now facing a similar problem.

In our particular case, we are dynamically rendering components like this:

```
const factory = resolver.resolveComponentFactory(component);
compRef = viewContainer.createComponent(factory);
```
